when guardians of the galaxy had  theaters in 2014 audiences immediately  fell in love with Drax the destroyer  played to perfection by Dave Bautista  Drax was Batista's Hollywood breakout  but this wasn't his first taste of  celebrity years before stepping into the  Marvel Cinematic Universe Dave Bautista  was one of the most famous wrestlers in  the WWE known simply as Batista but how  did he go from the WWE to the MCU a  rough start  Dave Batista grew up in Washington DC  abandoned by his father  Batista credits his mother with pulling  them through difficult times and she  eventually took the family to San  Francisco as Batista grew older he found  himself involved with a pretty bad crowd  in addition to failing grades for teesta  was stealing cars by age 13 by the age  of 17 he was living on his own  working as a lifeguard before winding up  as a bouncer as he neared 30 Batista was  earning $100 a night in LA nightclubs  handling angry drunks while trying to  support his two kids finally fed up with  the way things were going  Batista decided it was time to make some  changes and tried to get into the  wrestling game however even though he  stood well over 6 feet tall and weighed  in at 340 pounds  Batista failed to impress when he  auditioned at WCW power plant but the  man who would be drags wasn't about to  give up instead he set his eye on a  different prize the WWE going prior as  someone had been getting into scrapes  since age 9 tossing guys around in a  cage seemed like a natural fit for  Batista he signed up with the wild  Samoan training center in Allentown and  after learning the ropes he made his way  to Ohio Valley Wrestling a feeder system  for World Wrestling Entertainment  Batista played a character called  Leviathan a demon raised from the Ohio  River the wrestler later described the  role as little cheesy but still cool  finally in 2002 WWE came calling  transforming Leviathan into deacon  batista a suit-wearing henchman to a  heel named reverend d-von admittedly  Batista was upset about the outfit as it  covered his body his strongest assets  eventually he dropped the Deacon bit and  became simply Batista joining up with  Triple H and Ric Flair to form the  wrestling super group known as evolution  soon Batista was strumming down with  Triple H at WrestleMania 21 where he  defeated his opponent  claim the world heavyweight championship  in 2005 in addition to setting a record  by holding the belt for 282 days Batista  would regain championship glory five  more times but ballpit ISTA was making a  name for himself not everything was  quite so happy behind the scenes leaving  the WWE despite his rise to stardom  Batista wasn't completely happy with his  newfound fame he started butting heads  with WWE owner Vince McMahon and grew  unhappy with the promotion's new PG era  the company brass wanted to tone down  the adult themes but Batista preferred  keeping things edgy Batista also didn't  feel like the WWE was giving him enough  opportunities outside the company he  wanted to score some acting gigs like  his WWE coworker John Cena but the  company wasn't interested in giving him  any juicy parts certain guys were  getting opportunities that I wasn't  getting and I wasn't real cool with that  so I left to accomplish certain things  feeling unloved by their promotion  Batista called it quits in 2010 and  while he returned for a few guest  appearances it seems he's largely put  his WWE days behind him getting started  as an actor before joining Marvel  Batista took some smaller roles playing  himself an Australian soap opera  neighbours and appearing in an episode  of Smallville but the acting bug didn't  really bite until he played a role in  the straight-to-dvd action flick wrong  side of town according to the budding  thespian he absolutely loved working on  the film but Bautista also had one  little problem as he told both movies  death I thought since I had done  on-camera stuff in WWE this was going to  be the same that it would be the same  stuff but then I realized how hard it  was deciding he had to get better  Bautista hide himself an acting coach  and started learning on the job he  learned from Billy Zane in the Scorpion  King 3 Dominic Purcell in House of the  Rising Sun and the future Guardians  co-star Vin Diesel and Riddick and all  that hard work eventually paid off when  director James Gunn started assembling a  ragtag bunch of space heroes to guard  the galaxy becoming Drax if you land a  major role in the MCU you've pretty much  got it made in the shade so it makes  sense up at easter was really anxious  about learning the parts of Drax the  destroyer a super literal bruiser  but Easter admitted to Wyatt that he was  terrified when trying out for the parts  after all this was the biggest projected  ever auditioned for but while he might  have been nerve  on the inside you wouldn't know by  watching a screen test auditioning  alongside Chris Pratt's Batista appears  pretty chill and incredibly natural as  the otherworldly assassin okay I got you  back I won't touch you again that's the  last time I touch you despite his long  show business career for teesta was  still pretty nervous when he showed up  for work on guardians of the galaxy he  described that first day as  nerve-wracking but eventually he started  feeling at home with his Marvel co-stars  describing Zoe Saldana and Chris Pratt  as world-class actors but the real  challenge was to make obsessions it  usually took four to six hours for the  makeup crew to get Bautista ready for  the day he wasn't too crazy about  spending day after day in all that  makeup eventually it would start to  irritate the skin and he told Collider  it made him quote constantly filled  dirty as for the finished product  Bautista was pretty critical of his  performance at first but as he watched  the film unfold he was totally drawn  into the movie life after guardians  since he saved the galaxy the first time  around Bautista has been keeping himself  pretty busy around Hollywood naturally  the actor reprised his role as tracks  and guardians of the galaxy vol 2 and  Avengers infinity war but Bautista has  been doing a lot more than just Marvel  work in 2015 he played mr. Hanks  Inspector Blofeld's terrifying henchmen  who gives James Bond one of the best  brawls in the entire double-oh-seven  franchise the man also put his martial  art skills to work in kick boxer  vengeance playing an undefeated body by  the name of Tong PO and put in a  supporting turn in Blade Runner 2049  before co-starring with Sylvester  Stallone in a skate planter the WWE's  lost was Tinseltown's gained and it  looks like Batista will be winning  hearts and bashing skulls on the silver  screen for a very long time  [Music]
 

